{
  "_comment": "Canonical line categories. Each carries its own AME eligibility and the clause that grounds it, which is what makes step 5 a table lookup rather than a pile of conditionals — and what makes every finding automatically citable. Roughly 70 categories: the payable classes a hospital bill is itemised into, plus the IRDAI non-payable list (Master Circular 2024, Annexure II) and the items its Annexures III and IV subsume into room or procedure charges — which are not separately payable, so they carry annexure II here too. Aliases are the tier-1 lexicon (§14): exact after normalisation, then trigram-fuzzy above the calibrated threshold. An alias must be unambiguous on its own; a phrase that could name two categories belongs to neither.",
