  "_comment_PHARMACY": "Split from consumables deliberately. Circular 151/06/2020 §3(i) excludes 'pharmacy and consumables' from AME as one phrase, so both categories carry AME.EXCL.PHARMA. But they differ on the independent question of payability: prescribed drugs administered during treatment are payable, while disposables are the classic Annexure II item a consumables rider exists to buy back. One combined category would have had to pick one answer, and picking 'non-payable' would mean telling every policyholder their medicines were lawfully disallowed. Note what is NOT here: neither category claims the alias 'pharmacy & consumables'. A bill line billed as that single lump genuinely is ambiguous between a payable and a non-payable category, so it must route to UNRESOLVED / AMBIGUOUS_DESCRIPTION and be corrected against the hospital's itemisation. Giving the alias to either category would resolve the ambiguity by fiat in whichever direction we happened to choose.",
